sequenceDiagram
  %% Current runner flow inside stage 3. Swamp reaches the task copy through its Node and runs as agent in the copy. One shared runner checks the real CLI and effects on the nested fleet. The verification-cases reference owns scheduling and case syntax; proof and proof:run own reset and cleanup policy.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 3 · proof runner
  %% kind: pipeline.3-proof-runner
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane CP icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane NT icon=server pill=fleet tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>verify workflow
  participant CP as Task copy<br/>runner as agent
  participant NT as Nested fleet<br/>Gateway · 2 Nodes
  GW->>SW: Start the verify run<br/>copy · cases · assignments
  SW->>CP: Select the cases<br/>runner plan --lines
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - validates definitions and emits batches in declared order; a plan is not a runtime verdict
  CP-->>SW: Ordered plan<br/>batches · cases
  loop each assigned batch
    opt the batch requires a reset
      SW->>CP: Reset the inner fleet<br/>base · apply · readiness
      %%> When:
      %%> - orbit proof resets every batch; proof:run resets its first batch and each batch after one that can change the fleet
      %%> On failure:
      %%> - no cases start; missing cases are unrun with cause infrastructure
    end
    SW->>CP: Run setup and batch<br/>shared runner
    CP->>NT: Prepare prerequisites<br/>Gateway · observers · callers
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - uses the candidate's pinned Ansible collections and scoped grants; records the tested revision and prepares the proof-only static CLI catalog
    %%> - prepares observer versions and fresh reports, then caller checkout mounts, home, CA and profile before scheduling cases
    %%> - batch and direct case calls require preparation even if setup already ran; failure starts no case
    opt declared batch setup
      CP->>NT: Set the batch start state<br/>declared setup steps
    end
    loop cases under runner locks
      CP->>NT: Set up the case<br/>declared resources
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - readers may share a Node; a writer holds its target through the case; shared-fleet and unresolved write scopes run alone
      %%> - cases use their own resources and undo nothing; no reset follows a failed case within a batch
      CP->>NT: Run the real CLI<br/>candidate checkout
      CP->>NT: Check the effect<br/>typed result · real state
      %%> Result:
      %%> - assertions check the case's observable outcome, not just exit zero or an Operation status
    end
    CP-->>SW: Verdict per case<br/>full result artifact
    %%> Result:
    %%> - passed, failed or unrun, with cause, checks and timing; the 4 KiB history tail is not the report
  end
  alt every selected case passed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>complete verdicts
  else a case failed or did not run
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed or unrun cases
  end
